<title>UK: UK crown prosecution service takes over Regan case.</title>
<headline>UK crown prosecution service takes over Regan case.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Co-Operative Wholesale Society (CWS) said on Tuesday its private criminal prosecution against entrepreneur Andrew Regan has been taken over by Britain's Crown Prosecution Service.</p>
<p>CWS said in a statement that the CPS has asked the police to undertake further investigations into the case brought by the supermarkets-to-funeral parlours group against Regan, who in April failed in a 1.2 billion pound ($2 billion) bid attempt for the CWS.</p>
</text>
